As you make your way past the cold stone walls of the ruins, you notice the 
complete lack of any noises one would expect of the jungle. It seems as if 
even the proximity to these ruins illicits a reverence from all of the sundry
creations which wander freely around this divine sanctuary. The jungle 
encroaches close to the wall, but it remains untoppled after what appear to
be years of growth. This gives you pause as you wonder what could make such a 
place so protected and revered and yet completely forgotten and left to the
whim of nature.
